f  you're confronted by this nightmare well  this is the advice given to residents in  Granville Tower told to stay put in  their flat unless a fire actually  reached them many chose to ignore this  they chose to flee I've opened a window  and I heard some woman's scene is  getting bigger is getting bigger so I've  gone out to the hallway I've looked for  this fire oh I see smoke everywhere I've  opened the door and the neighbors were  the end and the people screaming the  firemen didn't get down the stairs so I  grabbed a little girl grab my girlfriend  Rena anyhow I heard a lot of screams and  I could see Alfre hand side I was  looking up and I could see people  bending on the windows and it was fire  all around him it was horrendous we saw  people from the 14th floor crying people  from the 16th floor my neighbor his aunt  was struggling I told him where's your  dad because I know his dad and he said  to me he's indoors he can't walk a  certain let's go and when we went try to  get in the Marcus know where you can get  me I was going through the floor the  fire brigade we had their oxygen we  never had the oxygen so what just have  to leave so there were firefighters  inside the building evacuated just came  in tried to evacuate the people telling  them to God but he told us to stay in  but I have to open the door and to get  out there's a lot of people on the upper  floors  flashing their torch lights and the most  upsetting thing about it all was  you could you could make out there was a  couple of young kids with flashlights  waving waving at people to try and help  them you can hear a lot of screaming  saying help me please please please and  it's just really emotional and sad to  hear  daylight comes early at this time of  year what we saw was hammering around  the tower a carpet of debris charred  possessions but also the industrial  cladding that had burnt from around the  building hundreds of emergency personnel  but inside look to the left of your  screen you can see what appears to be a  resident still in their flat peering out  while three storeys above them this  building burns we don't know what  happened to this person but a story  that's been told repeatedly is one of  utter desperation of people in this  tower trapped and jumping for their  lives  I did see a few people jump people were  jumping and I think at that point it was  you leave a jump in trying to save your  life you might break a few bones or get  engulfed in that flame I saw two people  jump from the right-hand side from I  think I have a froth from 10 to 15 I  couldn't tell you which broad I couldn't  tell you if there were adult so I  couldn't tell you if they were kids or  teenagers all I could see is two people  flinging themselves off the thing people  were telling me other people are doing  it on the other on the other side as  well  there's just one staircase one in one  outside if you can't get to them  staircase you are not getting out that  building there's only one way out that  building unless the jump being trapped  in a burning building is many people's  idea of a nightmare for some there was  relief in simply surviving want to wake  you but for others the trauma of  separation of not knowing what has  happened to friends and to loved ones  the woman sounds like calm she wasn't  panicked or anything and I said what is  your husband she said he's talking to  the emergency and I said waiting to come  out she said they tell us to stay in we  cannot come out and  I said what did they ask you to do she  said they asked us to cover the the  doors with towels and she said but the  fire is coming heavily and then about I  think 1015 minute later we phoned them  back and I said where is your husband  she said he's still talking and they  said they're coming to us and I said  what happened she said the last thing  she said smoke is coming heavily through  the door into the flat that was the last  time could you just sent out a message  about 12 hours ago to say that she was  trapped and that everybody should pray  for her we've been to every single place  that they've asked us to go to  we've separate our families in two  different places some are contacting  hospitals and we're just wandering on to  look for them since this morning who's  helping no one we're doing it ourselves  and behind them the flames burnt on  relentlessly the capital's worst Inferno  for many many years  a unprecedented incident in my 29 years  of being a firefighter I have never ever  seen anything of this scale our first  fire engines were unseen in under six  minutes crews wearing breathing  apparatus and extended duration  breathing apparatus have been working in  extremely challenging and very difficult  conditions to rescue people and to bring  this major fire under control  at this time I am very sad to confirm  that there have been a number of  fatalities  ESCOs amidst the trauma and the grief  the best side of humanity emerged to  people and organizations rushing to  offer food water clothes and shelter  many thousands of pounds have already  been pledged to help and that sum is  growing very rapidly the questions that  will now follow and not just about how  this fire started but why it grew so  huge and so  fast and if that can happen to Grenville  tower could it happen somewhere else the  focus of the experts today  is the search and rescue very soon I'm  afraid I'll move on to recovery but  there are genuine concerns reasonable  concerns that have been raised through  the course of the night and it's really  important that these questions are  answered this building has just been  refurbished a process that took around  two years and cost millions of pounds  but residents here have long alleged  it's unsafe just seven months ago  one group predicted a catastrophic event  a prediction that today came grimly true  there was an issue a few years ago where  there was a small fire and there was  concerns from the TMO residents  regarding this building and the safety  of this building there was a lot of  worries and this was one of the worries  that one day that something like this  could happen  Grenville Tower was built to the  standards of the 1970s just one  staircase no central alarm and no  sprinkler system investigators will want  to know if the cladding put around it  resisted a fire or made it worse there  has been a response from Ryden the  company that did the building work it  said we will cooperate with the relevant  authorities and emergency services and  fully support their inquiries into the  causes of this fire at the appropriate  time the government has set checks will  be carried out into all tower blocks  that had similar refurbishments  there has been heroism today and people  have survived an appalling experience  but many others have died and lessons  will have to be learnt a knight who  shocking events will reverberate for a  very long time  Adam Parsons Sky News
 

